{% assign rawPluginName = pluginName | replace_first: "rp1-", "" -%}
version: 1.0.0
title: rp1-{{ rawPluginName }}-{{ artifact.name }}
description: {{ artifact.description | escape_yaml }}
instructions: |
  You are running an rp1-generated Goose recipe.
  Use the generated skill at `{% raw %}{{ recipe_dir }}{% endraw %}/../skills/{{ artifact.namespacedName }}/SKILL.md` as the authoritative instructions.
  The generated entrypoint is `goose run --recipe <this file>`{% if artifact.metadata and artifact.metadata.arguments and artifact.metadata.arguments.size > 0 %} with `--params ARGUMENTS='<raw rp1 arguments>'` when arguments are needed{% endif %}.
  If that skill file is missing, stop and tell the user to rebuild Goose artifacts with `rp1 build:opencode --platform goose`.
  Before running the rp1 workflow, use the developer shell to run `goose --version`, parse the first semantic version, and verify it is at least `{{ platformConfig.min_version }}`.
  If Goose is older than `{{ platformConfig.min_version }}`, or if the version cannot be checked, stop without running the rp1 workflow and report: `Goose {{ platformConfig.min_version }} or newer is required for rp1 generated recipes; found <version or error>. Upgrade Goose and rerun this recipe.`
  When generated skill instructions ask for `CURRENT_HOST`, use `goose`.
  When generated skill instructions ask for basic filesystem or shell capabilities (`Read`, `Write`, `Edit`, `Grep`, `Glob`, or `Bash`), use the builtin `developer` extension. If the developer extension is unavailable, stop and report: `Goose developer extension is required for rp1 generated recipes. Re-run with the developer extension enabled.`
{%- if artifact.unsupportedTools and artifact.unsupportedTools.size > 0 %}
  This recipe's generated skill declares unsupported Goose tools: {{ artifact.unsupportedTools | join: ", " }}. If the requested run requires any of these capabilities, stop before following the skill and report: `Goose unsupported capability: {{ artifact.unsupportedTools | join: ", " }} are not supported in this build. Run this workflow on a compatible harness.`
{%- endif %}
  Treat Goose JSON output as a transcript or metadata envelope, not as a bare final answer. Inspect the final assistant message or structured event metadata deliberately before deciding that a workflow completed.
  Delegation, nested delegation, interactive approvals, user elicitation, web access, notebook editing, and background shell session control are unsupported in this build unless the generated instruction says a validated foreground Summon smoke exists. If one of those capabilities is required, stop and report the unsupported capability instead of waiting or pretending it succeeded.
  If an rp1 command fails, report the exact error and the recovery step from the command output.
prompt: |
  Run the generated rp1 skill `{{ artifact.namespacedName }}`.
{%- if artifact.metadata and artifact.metadata.arguments and artifact.metadata.arguments.size > 0 %}

  The recipe parameter `ARGUMENTS` contains the raw rp1 arguments string:
  {% raw %}{{ ARGUMENTS }}{% endraw %}

  Before following any generated shell snippet that references `$ARGUMENTS`, assign that value to the shell variable `ARGUMENTS`.

  Declared rp1 arguments:
{%- for arg in artifact.metadata.arguments %}
  - {{ arg.name }} ({% if arg.required %}required{% else %}optional{% endif %}): {{ arg.description }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- endif %}

  Start by reading the generated skill file, then follow it exactly.
  If the generated skill reports `Goose unsupported capability`, stop and return that message as the recipe result.
extensions:
  - type: builtin
    name: developer
    display_name: Developer
    timeout: 300
    bundled: true
{%- if artifact.metadata and artifact.metadata.arguments and artifact.metadata.arguments.size > 0 %}
parameters:
  - key: ARGUMENTS
    input_type: string
    requirement: optional
    default: ""
    description: Raw argument string for the generated rp1 skill, for example FEATURE_ID=goose-harness-core
{%- endif %}
